    feat(board): a dispatch door, so a round can be started from the interface
    
    The board declares a milestone, issues GO and runs a gate, but nothing on it could
    run a round, so there was no way to start S1 through the surface the owner uses.
    This calls round.dispatch -- the same verb the CLI and the HTTP transport call --
    so it is a door onto the one entry point, not a second one.
    
    The task row reaches its project through milestone, and outcome lands in
    narrative; both were guesses until the schema said otherwise.

